Functions for Manipulating Individual Bits
Functions for Manipulating Individual Bits
SimTalk provides the functions listed in the table of contents to the left for manipulating individual bits of
an integer value.
Functions for Manipulating Individual Bits
12-314 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

BitAND [SimTalk]
Executes a bitwise AND of value 1 and value 2 and returns the result.
Type
Function
Syntax
BitAND(Value1:integer, Value2:integer) → integer
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Value1 of data type integer designates value 1.
• The parameter Value2 of data type integer designates value 2.
Return Value
The return value has the data type integer.
BitAND [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-315
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

BitClear [SimTalk]
Changes the value of the parameter OriginalValue by setting the bit with the number designated by the
parameter BitPosition to the bit value 0. The function returns the result of this computation.
Type
Function
Syntax
BitClear(OriginalValue:integer, BitPosition:integer) → integer
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter OriginalValue of data type integer designates the original value of the computation.
• The parameter BitPosition of data type integer designates the bit position. The value range for the bit
position is 0 to 63. The least significant bit has the number 0, the most significant bit has the number
63.
Return Value
The return value has the data type integer.
See also
BitSet [SimTalk]
BitClear [SimTalk]
12-316 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

BitOR [SimTalk]
Executes a bitwise OR of value 1 and value 2 and returns the result.
Type
Function
Syntax
BitOR(Value1:integer, Value2:integer) → integer
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Value1 of data type integer designates value 1.
• The parameter Value2 of data type integer designates value 2.
Return Value
The return value has the data type integer.
BitOR [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-317
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

BitSet [SimTalk]
Changes the value of the parameter OriginalValue by setting the bit with the number designated by the
parameter BitPosition to the bit value 1. The function returns the result of this computation.
Type
Function
Syntax
BitSet(OriginalValue:integer, BitPosition:integer) → integer
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter OriginalValue of data type integer designates the original value of the computation.
• The parameter BitPosition of data type integer designates the bit position. The value range for the bit
position is 0 to 63. The least significant bit has the number 0, the most significant bit has the number
63.
Return Value
The return value has the data type integer.
See also
BitClear [SimTalk]
BitSet [SimTalk]
12-318 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

BitShift [SimTalk]
Shifts the bits of the value designated by the parameter integer using the number of digits designated by
integer and returns the result.
Type
Function
Syntax
BitShift(Value:integer, NumberOfDigits:integer) → integer
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Value of data type integer designates the value.
• The parameter NumberOfDigits of data type integer designates number of digits. It moves them to the
left, if you specified digits greater than 0. It moves them to the right, if you specified digits smaller than
0.
Return Value
The return value has the data type integer.
BitShift [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-319
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

BitTest [SimTalk]
Returns if in the Value the bit at the position designated by BitPosition is set (true) or not (false).
Type
Function
Syntax
BitTest(Value:integer, BitPosition:integer) → boolean
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Value of data type integer designates the value.
• The parameter BitPosition of data type integer designates the bit position. The value range for the bit
position is 0 to 63. The least significant bit has the number 0, the most significant bit has the number
63.
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
Example
var i : integer := 40 // binary representation: 00101000
print bitTest(i, 3)   // returns true because the bit 3 is set
BitTest [SimTalk]
12-320 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

BitXOR [SimTalk]
Executes a bitwise XOR of value 1 and value 2 and returns the result.
Type
Function
Syntax
BitXOR(Value1:integer, Value2:integer) → integer
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Value1 of data type integer designates value 1.
• The parameter Value2 of data type integer designates value 2.
Return Value
The return value has the data type integer.
Functions for Manipulating Strings
Functions for Editing Variables of Data Type String
SimTalk provides the functions listed in the table of contents to the left for editing variables of data type
string.
These functions do not change the contents of the strings, but work with copies of the strings. The result
of this operation is the return value. This enables Plant Simulation to enter names of objects into message
texts during a simulation run.
BitXOR [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-321
